<title>BRAZIL: Brazil IBGE ups wheat estimate to 2.9 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Brazil IBGE ups wheat estimate to 2.9 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil should produce 2.9 million tonnes of wheat in 1997, down 11.67 percent from last year but up 11.01 percent from the previous estimate, according to National Statistics Institute (IBGE).</p>
<p>The increase in the latest forecast is due to new production detected in Parana and Goias states, IBGE said.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
